Id: core-ltx25
Title: Add support for LTX-2.5 (22B, Gemma-4 text encoder)
Does: Lets the renderer load the LTX-2.5 family: its int8-convrot 22B transformer, the new
 gemma4-12b-with-proj text encoder (loaded through the LTXV two-file clip path / LTXVAudioTextEncoderLoader,
 which now detects Gemma-4 as well as Gemma-3), the reworked LTXAV diffusion model, the neural-adaptive VAE
 decoder and the duration head. Without it LTX-2.5's Gemma-4 encoder has no load path (the existing LTXAV
 encoder is hardwired to Gemma-3) and the model cannot run.
Target: .
Base: comfyanonymous/ComfyUI
Why: A verbatim cherry-pick of upstream ComfyUI commit 57ce8e1a27dda3d4cedab081081fd3e1359c195b
 ("Add support for LTX 2.5", PR #15499), whose parent is exactly this build's pinned COMFYUI_REF
 (62b3c94bd45154f6486c7abf1b9efcacee96ea69), so the diff applies with zero offset. LTX-2.5 support lives
 only on master and no tagged release carries it yet; rather than move the comfy pin onto an unreleased
 branch, we carry the single enabling commit here until it lands in a release we can pin to.
---
